    "goal": "Culture a human proximal-tubule channel that reproduces the canonical in vivo apical fluid shear of 0.2 dyn/cm² (0.02 Pa).",
    "rationale": "The canonical published apical shear for proximal-tubule epithelial cells is 0.2 dyn/cm², which converts to 0.02 Pa (×0.1). Using a typical proximal-tubule-on-chip rectangular channel (400 µm wide × 100 µm high), the flow rate required to hit 0.02 Pa wall shear is 0.8 µL/min (computed via flow_rate_for_shear_stress). This flow gives Re ≈ 0.05 (deeply laminar) and a pressure drop of only ~8 Pa over 20 mm, well within syringe-pump capability. No proximal-tubule entry exists in the physiology registry, so the shear target rests on the user-provided canonical value rather than a registry range.",
